## Gap 1: `@ts-nocheck` Debt — Claim is Completely Stale

> [!TIP]
> The report claimed **50+ server files** use `@ts-nocheck`. A full regex search of the entire codebase shows **zero instances** in any [.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/shared/pips.ts) server file.

The only occurrences found in the entire repo:
| File | Context |
|------|---------|
| [db/fixSchema.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/db/fixSchema.ts) | Database migration script (not server runtime) |
| `REPORTS AND REVIEWS/routes.BACKUP REFERENCE-DO NOT EDIT.ts` | Dead backup file |
| [client/vite.plugins/autoI18n.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/vite.plugins/autoI18n.ts) | Build tooling regex (detection, not suppression) |

**Verdict:** The `@ts-nocheck` technical debt has been **fully resolved** since the report was written. The report's recommendations around removing `@ts-nocheck` during refactors are moot.

